pyannote speaker-diarization-community-1
========================================

The files in this release are those of pyannote's speaker diarization pipeline
"speaker-diarization-community-1", without any modification:

  Work     : pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1
  Authors  : pyannote (pyannoteAI, Hervé Bredin and contributors)
  Source   : https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1
  Revision : 3533c8cf8e369892e6b79ff1bf80f7b0286a54ee
  License  : Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0),
             full text in the LICENSE file of this release,
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Greffier (https://github.com/FredeAlexandre/greffier) republishes them here, as
is, so that the app can download them without a Hugging Face account. Only the
file names change, because a GitHub release has no folders:

  config.yaml                     → config.yaml
  segmentation-pytorch_model.bin  → segmentation/pytorch_model.bin
  embedding-pytorch_model.bin     → embedding/pytorch_model.bin
  plda-plda.npz                   → plda/plda.npz
  plda-xvec_transform.npz         → plda/xvec_transform.npz

The pipeline is used with pyannote.audio (https://github.com/pyannote/pyannote-audio,
MIT license).
